ch as 1.3 million dollars a day if we  didn't follow what they would ask us to  do  since you won in the Supreme Court if  you work at Hobby Lobby it does not  cover contraceptive care that's correct  it does yes the 16 contraceptives we do  supply but not these four that would be  after the fact there was some research  that said that hobby lobby's 401k plan  invests in certain pharmaceuticals that  presume that that develop those very  drugs that you're opposed to is that  hypocritical no it's not hypocritical  because it'd be like me going into a  drug store and I'm seeing things in  there that I wouldn't buy but I still  have to be part of that but it would be  a very very very small percent of  anybody's 401 and if I didn't offer  different things other than one that  would be a pure 401 then I would get  tremendous criticism that I'm I'm  cutting my employees investments down to  suit me you pay about double the federal  minimum wage to your employees correct  that's correct our minimum wage is  fifteen dollars and seventy cents for  our full-time employees so how would you  feel about the government enacting  legislation that requires the federal  minimum wage to be fifteen dollars I  don't think that would be fair I think  that would be that needs to be up to the  very businesses and I think that they  want to pay five dollars an hour that's  okay with you well you cannot do that  because of the competition you cannot  hire people at five dollars an hour so  there's certain amount of competition  out there as well as a lot of young  people wouldn't have job was the  competition led you to pay fifteen  dollars no no it wasn't but we decided  to do this on our own but we certainly  couldn't pay $5.00 yeah it was a you  wanted it to be a market based decision  that the employer could make the choice  and look you're gonna recruit better and  retain better exactly by paying and that  was a decision there but we're not  suggesting the government comes in and  req